From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Momplet <mompletvictor@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:27:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(training): a gym session's calories and Effort count the
 lifting, and catch up with the strap

A 70-minute weights session read 263 kcal and Effort 18/100: both came from
heart rate alone, which barely rises with heavy short sets, and when the
workout was saved before the strap handed over its heart rate they were also
scored on part of the window and never again (upstream only rescores a manual
workout that has under 5 kcal or no Effort).

- Claude's estimate now also gives the session's Effort on the app's 0-100
  axis with the muscular load of the sets added to what the heart rate
  measured (as WHOOP's Strength Trainer does), never below the heart-rate one.
- The workout row takes the session's figures: calories = the larger of
  Claude's and the heart-rate estimate, Effort = the larger of the two, heart
  rate as freshly scored, so the list, the detail and the totals show them.
  The day's balance keeps using the heart-rate figure the analysis saw, so
  nothing is counted twice.
- Sessions of the last three days are analysed again when their window holds
  clearly more heart-rate samples than their analysis saw (a quarter more and
  at least a minute), or when they were never analysed; checked when Today,
  Food or a workout shows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
